      {
        "id": 114962,
        "name": "McBehrer",
        "username": "McBehrer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-15T17:54:01.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Honestly, and I know this isn't much help, I just memorized the cards.</p><p>All of them.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thankfully, there aren't many \"when you do something, do this\" effects; at least not many that can be in play at the same time. Time Cataclysm is the worst one, and you can only have 1 of those out at a time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What I'd suggest is just assign a person to watch for a particular trigger. Something like, \"Joe, Interpolation Beam just entered play. Remind us to take damage whenever we draw cards.\"</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:47:00.218Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
