      {
        "id": 114964,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-15T19:28:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>As Spiff mentioned, I'll use reminders (although I have a box of various tokens from other games, etc., that I use). I'll drop a token in an appropriate place to remind me there's something to remember. For example, if there's a trigger on a villain card being destroyed, I'll put a token on the villain trash, then everytime I have to pick it up to put a card in the trash I know to check.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I've also found it useful when one of the players chooses a specific trigger they will \"catch\", always watching for that trigger. Sometimes, there's one person who's just more focused and capable at that kind of thing and they do it well.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
